# SubtleForms: standing rules

You work on ONE package at a time. The package file in docs/dev/packages/ is your whole task. Do not audit, refactor, rename or "improve" anything outside it.

## Read only what you need
- Your package file lists every bug with repro, expected result, actual result and likely cause (file:line from server 1.6.0; line numbers may have moved, search for the function).
- Open the full QA report in docs/dev/qa/ only if a bug row is unclear. Evidence paths in those reports point to the auditor's machine and are not in this repo.
- docs/dev/bug-ledger.csv maps every bug ID to its release and package. Never work on IDs that are not in your package.

## Branch and commits
- Branch: `pkg/<PACKAGE-ID>` from the release branch named in the package file. One commit per bug ID (or per tightly related group), message: `<ID>[, <ID>]: <what changed, plain sentence>`.
- Never commit build/, dist/, node_modules/, vendor/ or playwright-report/. Never push to main. Open a pull request into the release branch when done.
- Agents must never merge, push to main, tag, or deploy. Humans merge only when docs/dev/MERGING.md is satisfied.
- No AI or tool attribution anywhere in git or GitHub: no `Co-Authored-By` lines, no "Generated with" or "Created by" lines, no tool or model names in commit messages, PR titles or PR bodies. Write them as plain notes from the team.

## Code rules
- PHP 8.1+, WordPress coding standards, classes prefixed `SFLS_`, prefix `sfls_` for functions, options, transients, hooks and handles. Text domain `subtleforms-license-server`.
- Sanitize input, escape output, nonces and capability checks on every route and admin action, `$wpdb->prepare` (use `%i` for identifiers). Server checks whatever the browser checks.
- Admin UI follows the existing screens. Sentence case. Plain words. No em dashes anywhere (code comments, UI copy, readme, changelog).
- Do not add dependencies. Do not change the database schema unless the package says so.

## Done means
1. Every bug ID in the package is fixed at its cause, with a regression test in `tests/integration` that failed before and passes now.
2. The integration suite passes: `SFLS_WP_PATH=/path/to/wordpress phpunit -c phpunit.xml` on a disposable WordPress with WooCommerce and this plugin active. If you cannot run it, say so in the report.
3. Changelog: add ONE new file `docs/dev/changes/unreleased/<short-branch-slug>.md` with the first line `type: Added|Changed|Fixed|Security` and one plain sentence below it (format in docs/dev/changes/README.md). A pull request with no user-visible change adds none.

## Files only a release pull request edits
Feature and fix pull requests must NOT edit `readme.txt`, `docs/dev/releases/`, the version in `subtleforms-license-server.php`, or `languages/*.pot`. Two pull requests that edit those lines conflict on every merge. The release pull request (`release/<version>`) bumps the version, runs `bin/compile-changes.sh <version> --apply` and regenerates the POT as its last step. The exact commands are in docs/dev/RELEASING.md. Pull requests run GitHub Actions Checks (see docs/dev/MERGING.md and BRANCH_PROTECTION.md): that is code CI for this plugin. Ingesting Pro zips, signing, yank/publish on subtleforms.com, and customer update delivery are production operations and require explicit human authorization.

## Report (keep it short; this is the only thing to write back)
```
Package: <ID>   Branch: pkg/<ID>   PR: <url>
Fixed: <ID> <one line each>
Tests added: <files>  Results: integration <n>/<n>
Not fixed: <ID> <reason>   (empty if none)
Touched outside package: <files and why>   (empty if none)
```
